ou pass the driving exam?\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Move the words from the box to correctly complete the sentences.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 9, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le12ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nDiscuss situations that relate to superstitions.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Anecdotes and Personal Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Man Named Leo", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About the Past: The Simple Past, The Present Perfect and the Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you tell stories and anecdotes, it is common to use a mixture of tenses. This allows you to convey a variety of timelines and action sequences.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Simple Past tense</span>  to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Suddenly he <span class=\"strong\">saw </span> a black cat. <br/> He immediately <span class=\"strong\">turned </span> the corner and <span class=\"strong\">stepped </span> into a narrow alley.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. It is common to use <span class=\"italic\">for </span> and <span class=\"italic\">since </span> when referring to time periods in the Present Perfect.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">Leo <span class=\"strong\">has always been</span>  superstitious. People <span class=\"strong\">have believed </span> these things <span class=\"strong\">for </span> many generations.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Past Continuous tense </span> to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now and to describe the background in a story written in the past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">When Leo turned into the alley, he <span class=\"strong\">was heading </span> under the ladder at full speed!  That's when he noticed the ladder <span class=\"strong\">was standing</span>  there. </span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Third Conditional - Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about situations that could have happened in the past, but did not.<br/> You often use the third conditional to speculate about how past events could have been different.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about situations in the past in a hypothetical context (not real or necessarily true), you use the structures <span class=\"italic\">could/would have + past participle.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If Tom <span class=\"strong\">hadn't broken </span> Tanya's fall, they never <span class=\"strong\">would have met</span>.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span>  + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hadn't noticed </span> the ladder, he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wouldn't have looked </span> up.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " If he hadn't looked up he wouldn't have noticed the young woman, who we all know as Tanya now, losing her balance. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If he hadn't thought quickly, she could have been badly injured. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "superstitious ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having beliefs rooted in magic rather than human logic or science", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Leo has always been superstitious.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about superstitions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "narrow ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not wide; a short distance from one side to the other", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He turned the corner and stepped into a narrow alley.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "alley", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a narrow street between buildings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He  stepped into a narrow alley, safely avoiding the black cat.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to realize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to  notice or understand something that you didn't know before", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He did not realize at first that something was happening in the alley. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "old wives' tale", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advice \u200bbelieved correct in the past but now \u200bknown to be \u200bwrong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He believes all the old wives' tales he hears.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of superstitions or old wives' tales that you, friends, or other people in your family think about when you do things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the superstitions and say what the people do. (<span class=\"italic\">When I spill the salt, I throw some over my left shoulder.</span>) Try for 8 of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now recount the superstition and what the person does by using hypothetical statements. (<span class=\"italic\">If I had spilled the salt, I would have ...</span> )", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your statements with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write down superstitions and what people do because of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the third conditional to recount what people would do hypothetically.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my hypothetical statements with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}